{
 "section_summary": "This section contains English translations and summaries of Japanese shortwave broadcasts from September and October 1941, enclosed with FBI letters to the State Department. The broadcasts report the formation of Hideki Tojo’s cabinet, Japanese operations in China and French Indochina, and the German invasion of the Soviet Union. Their commentary promotes Japan’s Greater East Asia policy and portrays Britain, the United States, and the Chongqing government as weak or divided.",
